    "body": "Hi @amjhou, thanks for the detailed build delta and A/B comparison!\n\nSince this only triggers over long multi-turn agentic sessions on the hybrid architecture, here are two quick checks that could help isolate the root cause between the kernel layer and prefix cache state management:\n\n1. **Test with prefix caching disabled:**\n   Try running the server with `--no-enable-prefix-caching`. In multi-turn agentic workloads where conversation histories are continuously appended, prefix caching interacts closely with hybrid / Mamba SSM recurrent state restoration. If disabling prefix caching eliminates the token degeneration, it points to prefix cache hit / state indexing in the hybrid KV cache manager.\n\n2. **Pin FlashInfer to `0.6.17`:**\n   Try downgrading FlashInfer on the bad build (`pip install flashinfer-python==0.6.17`). Testing this will immediately isolate whether the regression comes from the recent FlashInfer 0.6.18 attention kernel update or from vLLM core commits.\n\nCurious to hear if either of these helps narrow down the regression on your end!",
